### AdaptiveColor struct and RGBA method

Source: https://github.com/charmbracelet/lipgloss

AdaptiveColor returns Dark.RGBA() when HasDarkBackground is true, else Light.RGBA(). Fields are image/color.Color — pass lipgloss.Color(...) results (v1 accepted strings).

```go
type AdaptiveColor struct {
	Light color.Color
	Dark  color.Color
}

// color.go:57
func (c AdaptiveColor) RGBA() (uint32, uint32, uint32, uint32)
```

--------------------------------

### AdaptiveColor migration

Source: https://github.com/charmbracelet/lipgloss/blob/main/UPGRADE_GUIDE_V2.md

Shows migration of AdaptiveColor from v1 to v2 using compat or the recommended LightDark helper. Note that compat.AdaptiveColor takes color.Color values.

```go
// v1
color := lipgloss.AdaptiveColor{Light: "#0000ff", Dark: "#000099"}

// v2 — using compat (quick path)
color := compat.AdaptiveColor{
    Light: lipgloss.Color("#0000ff"),
    Dark:  lipgloss.Color("#000099"),
}

// v2 — using LightDark (recommended)
hasDark := lipgloss.HasDarkBackground(os.Stdin, os.Stdout)
lightDark := lipgloss.LightDark(hasDark)
color := lightDark(lipgloss.Color("#0000ff"), lipgloss.Color("#000099"))
```
